  "body": "PR891 already excludes positive whole-block single-write programs for R439\nframes 509 and 521, using two exhaustive order recursions. Four short integer\ninequalities now explain these exclusions independently of any realization\norder. Treating each donor's entry/final versions as mutually exclusive gives\nframe 509's wire 468 a required coefficient 3 against supply at most 2;\ntwo-coordinate functionals supply three analogous frame-521 witnesses.\n\nThe package pins the unchanged original word and PR891 statements/receipts,\nchecks all 23 rows and 6,118 small functionals, and independently reconstructs\nthe matrices by column execution and exhausts grouped donor choices. Exactly\nfour rows are infeasible; all 58,320 individually fitting combinations for\ntheir dual maxima are checked separately. Optimized isolated Python replay,\nrelocation and 12 mathematical/package controls pass.\n\nThe known exclusions belong to Aaron Wang (@navinor); this adds simpler\ncertificates and an explanation, not a new unrestricted circuit lower bound.\nMulti-write programs such as PR1015/1062 remain outside the restricted class.\nNo circuit, selected source, H1-H5 status, invoice or kappa changes. Prepared\nfor @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n",
